    },
    {
      "id": "tglR2jjIgGNR7XNBhWx9f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 608.9249092444757,
      "y": 761.2006892333997,
      "width": 574.5692123905355,
      "height": 540,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 416886429,
      "version": 1061,
      "versionNonce": 1859256851,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782882528496,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- 500 million DAU\n- Messages/day - 40\n- Average message size - 100 bytes (text + metadata)\n- Avg Grp size - 20 members\n- %age of grp msgs - 30%\n\n- 500M*40 = 20B+ msgs/day\n- 20B/86400 = 230,000 msgs/sec\n- Peak factor - 3x ~ 700,000 msgs/sec \n\nConnection\n- WebSockets\n- 10% DAU online at any time = 50M concurrent connections\n- Single server ~ 50K connections -> Peak ~ 100M\n- 50M/50K = 1000 chat servers -> Peak ~ 200M\n\nStorage\n- Msgs = 20B*100 bytes = 2TB/day\n- 2*365 = 730TB/yr\n- 730 TB/year is well within reach of distributed databases like\nCassandra or ScyllaDB (with replication, plan for roughly 3x)\n\nBandwidth\n- 230K msgs/sec * 100 bytes = 23MB/sec\n- Higher outbound as messages fan out to multiple devices\n- Modern network infrastructure handles this easily. Bandwidth is\nnot the bottleneck.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- 500 million DAU\n- Messages/day - 40\n- Average message size - 100 bytes (text + metadata)\n- Avg Grp size - 20 members\n- %age of grp msgs - 30%\n\n- 500M*40 = 20B+ msgs/day\n- 20B/86400 = 230,000 msgs/sec\n- Peak factor - 3x ~ 700,000 msgs/sec \n\nConnection\n- WebSockets\n- 10% DAU online at any time = 50M concurrent connections\n- Single server ~ 50K connections -> Peak ~ 100M\n- 50M/50K = 1000 chat servers -> Peak ~ 200M\n\nStorage\n- Msgs = 20B*100 bytes = 2TB/day\n- 2*365 = 730TB/yr\n- 730 TB/year is well within reach of distributed databases like Cassandra or ScyllaDB (with replication, plan for roughly 3x)\n\nBandwidth\n- 230K msgs/sec * 100 bytes = 23MB/sec\n- Higher outbound as messages fan out to multiple devices\n- Modern network infrastructure handles this easily. Bandwidth is not the bottleneck.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
