      "text": "KAFKA",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "UmMr4v-epD7gK3vvhODbD",
      "originalText": "KAFKA",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-oqQlD-54DYa0RLyQavWu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5623.659439925355,
      "y": 1248.8052794358332,
      "width": 941.0214833607924,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1687519636,
      "version": 373,
      "versionNonce": 1339700316,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784482682218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Create a Kafka topic for every user in the system. The idea here would be that we\ncould keep our Inbox table as a Kafka topic. Then our Chat Servers will subscribe to\nthe topic and deliver messages to the user.\nUnder this proposal, when a user connects to our Chat Server, they'd subscribe to the\ntopic for their user ID. When we need to send a message to a given user we'd publish\nthe message to the topic for that user. This message would be received by all the\nchat servers that have subscribed to that topic, and then the message could be passed\non to the websocket connection for that user.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Create a Kafka topic for every user in the system. The idea here would be that we could keep our Inbox table as a Kafka topic. Then our Chat Servers will subscribe to the topic and deliver messages to the user.\nUnder this proposal, when a user connects to our Chat Server, they'd subscribe to the topic for their user ID. When we need to send a message to a given user we'd publish the message to the topic for that user. This message would be received by all the chat servers that have subscribed to that topic, and then the message could be passed on to the websocket connection for that user.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "SWSMLT1dy4eTYnDIaFNsI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4764.518085381169,
