      "seed": 950769452,
      "version": 1799,
      "versionNonce": 1771970524,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784482682218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Zookeeper",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "H3qjjpbp0nmiAmsVR7A5k",
      "originalText": "Zookeeper",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KKbtcepKHEBIBW6q4Nf3k",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5610.110127159819,
      "y": 1762.0596822379434,
      "width": 941.0214833607924,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1275580844,
      "version": 527,
      "versionNonce": 690838876,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784482682218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Another approach for us to use is to always assign users to a specific Chat Server\nbased on their user ID. If we do this correctly, we'll always know which Chat Server\nis responsible for a given user so, when we need to send them messages, we can do so\ndirectly.\n\nKeep a central registry of how many Chat Servers we have, their addresses, and the\nwhich segments of a consistent hash space they own. Use a Zookeeper\nWhen a request comes in, we'll connect them to the Chat Server they are assigned to\nbased on their user id. When a new event is created, Chat Servers will connect\ndirectly with the Chat Server that \"owns\" that user id, then call an API which\ndelivers a notification the connected user (if they're connected).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Another approach for us to use is to always assign users to a specific Chat Server based on their user ID. If we do this correctly, we'll always know which Chat Server is responsible for a given user so, when we need to send them messages, we can do so directly.\n\nKeep a central registry of how many Chat Servers we have, their addresses, and the which segments of a consistent hash space they own. Use a Zookeeper\nWhen a request comes in, we'll connect them to the Chat Server they are assigned to based on their user id. When a new event is created, Chat Servers will connect directly with the Chat Server that \"owns\" that user id, then call an API which delivers a notification the connected user (if they're connected).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
