      "seed": 1557493468,
      "version": 499,
      "versionNonce": 1443781732,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784484212265,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Users often sit on poor network connections. The WebSocket may technically\nbe open, but the connection is functionally severed—we won't know until we\ntry to send a message and it times out. TCP keepalives can take minutes to\ndetect a dead connection, which is far too slow for a chat app. How can we\nmake sure our users aren't impacted?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Users often sit on poor network connections. The WebSocket may technically be open, but the connection is functionally severed—we won't know until we try to send a message and it times out. TCP keepalives can take minutes to detect a dead connection, which is far too slow for a chat app. How can we make sure our users aren't impacted?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6T1dNkKOUWZmacLoZK_ID",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8715.962881912998,
      "y": 1749.9911831230852,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 169090532,
      "version": 190,
      "versionNonce": 1290003676,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784485330482,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nDo nothing special. When the connection dies, TCP will\neventually time out and the socket will close. The client\nwill reconnect and sync from the Inbox.\n\nChallenges\n\nTCP keepalives are slow—often configured for minutes, not\nseconds. Users could be staring at a \"connected\" app that's\nactually dead, missing messages the whole time. Not\nacceptable for a real-time chat app.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nDo nothing special. When the connection dies, TCP will eventually time out and the socket will close. The client will reconnect and sync from the Inbox.\n\nChallenges\n\nTCP keepalives are slow—often configured for minutes, not seconds. Users could be staring at a \"connected\" app that's actually dead, missing messages the whole time. Not acceptable for a real-time chat app.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pnpj3skpoEExKAbZ0BTec",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8717.591163640871,
      "y": 1694.6258832858014,
      "width": 286,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1969663964,
      "version": 124,
      "versionNonce": 1821602020,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784484969987,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BAD : Rely on TCP Timeouts",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BAD : Rely on TCP Timeouts",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ghkjQnBGTYpQF2jcftlau",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9423.283018328908,
      "y": 1748.231264153532,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1143990364,
      "version": 271,
      "versionNonce": 848074460,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485335284,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nWhen Chat Server delivers a message over the WebSocket, it\nwaits for an ACK from the client.\nNo ACK within a short timeout (say, 500-2000ms), the server\nretries delivery. \nAfter a few failed retries, the server assumes the WebSocket\nis broken and closes it, forcing the client to reconnect and\nsync from the Inbox.\nThis pairs naturally with our existing client ACK mechanism\n(used to clear the Inbox). We're just adding a server-side\ntimeout to detect when the WebSocket has silently failed.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis only detects failures when we're actively trying to\nsend messages. If the connection dies during a quiet period,\nwe won't notice until the next message arrives.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nWhen Chat Server delivers a message over the WebSocket, it waits for an ACK from the client.\nNo ACK within a short timeout (say, 500-2000ms), the server retries delivery. \nAfter a few failed retries, the server assumes the WebSocket is broken and closes it, forcing the client to reconnect and sync from the Inbox.\nThis pairs naturally with our existing client ACK mechanism (used to clear the Inbox). We're just adding a server-side timeout to detect when the WebSocket has silently failed.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis only detects failures when we're actively trying to send messages. If the connection dies during a quiet period, we won't notice until the next message arrives.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HXe7dAWFNWUqKB68ulwFH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9424.911300056783,
      "y": 1692.8659643162482,
      "width": 462,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1867152604,
      "version": 231,
      "versionNonce": 440120420,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784484969987,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GOOD : ACK timeouts with server side retry",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GOOD : ACK timeouts with server side retry",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "bNcRrFclpEZfFdWmiLR8u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10158.642701200773,
      "y": 1744.2045960679372,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 626645988,
      "version": 388,
      "versionNonce": 223103196,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485339789,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nThe Chat Server sends periodic ping messages (every 10-30\nseconds) over the WebSocket. The client must respond with a\npong within a timeout (say, 5 seconds). If the client\ndoesn't respond, the server closes the connection.\nWhen the connection closes, the client reconnects and syncs\nany missed messages from the Inbox. This catches dead\nconnections within seconds rather than minutes.\n\nChallenges\n\nHeartbeats add overhead—with 200M connected users and a 10-\nsecond heartbeat interval, that's 20M ping/pong exchanges\nper second. In practice this is fine (they're tiny\nmessages), but it's worth noting.\nThe heartbeats give you a guaranteed upper bound on\ndetection time: if your heartbeat interval is 10s and\ntimeout is 5s, you'll detect any dead connection within 15\nseconds.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nThe Chat Server sends periodic ping messages (every 10-30 seconds) over the WebSocket. The client must respond with a pong within a timeout (say, 5 seconds). If the client doesn't respond, the server closes the connection.\nWhen the connection closes, the client reconnects and syncs any missed messages from the Inbox. This catches dead connections within seconds rather than minutes.\n\nChallenges\n\nHeartbeats add overhead—with 200M connected users and a 10-second heartbeat interval, that's 20M ping/pong exchanges per second. In practice this is fine (they're tiny messages), but it's worth noting.\nThe heartbeats give you a guaranteed upper bound on detection time: if your heartbeat interval is 10s and timeout is 5s, you'll detect any dead connection within 15 seconds.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OyUn1NIC8fRy6z19yAAwt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10160.270982928652,
      "y": 1688.8392962306534,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b30",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1694285668,
      "version": 349,
      "versionNonce": 17795044,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784484969987,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GREAT : Application-Level Heartbeats",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GREAT : Application-Level Heartbeats",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DUF8h85iPr3s_L3mmmvP7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7713.020335030803,
      "y": 2288.4074256250574,
      "width": 678.4397583007812,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b31",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 870695516,
      "version": 79,
      "versionNonce": 1307003876,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What happens if Redis fails to deliver a message?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What happens if Redis fails to deliver a message?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kV4aTaJ1Xgmvar_Yybjl5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7734.471869802479,
      "y": 2372.880639963285,
      "width": 769.928711967158,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b33",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1680440036,
      "version": 387,
      "versionNonce": 2052861796,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Redis Pub/Sub is \"at most once\"—if there's no subscriber listening or\nRedis has a transient failure, the message is lost. We've already\nhandled durability by writing to the Inbox before publishing to\nPub/Sub (importantly this means all messages will eventually get\ndelivered), but how do we ensure connected clients quickly receive\nmessages that Pub/Sub dropped?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Redis Pub/Sub is \"at most once\"—if there's no subscriber listening or Redis has a transient failure, the message is lost. We've already handled durability by writing to the Inbox before publishing to Pub/Sub (importantly this means all messages will eventually get delivered), but how do we ensure connected clients quickly receive messages that Pub/Sub dropped?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "T7GQ716rzpBVfCrBf5Vle",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8689.81865642498,
      "y": 2410.6752971718843,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b34",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1738832356,
      "version": 323,
      "versionNonce": 493396708,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nConnected clients periodically poll the server for missed\nmessages. Every 30-60 seconds, the client sends a \"sync\"\nrequest. The server checks the Inbox table for any\nundelivered messages and sends them down.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis adds load proportional to connected users. With 200M\nconnected users polling every 30 seconds, that's ~7M\nqueries/second just for sync checks. You can mitigate with\nlonger intervals, but you're trading latency for load.\nThe approach is \"good enough\" for most cases—the polling\ninterval is a tunable knob.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nConnected clients periodically poll the server for missed messages. Every 30-60 seconds, the client sends a \"sync\" request. The server checks the Inbox table for any undelivered messages and sends them down.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis adds load proportional to connected users. With 200M connected users polling every 30 seconds, that's ~7M queries/second just for sync checks. You can mitigate with longer intervals, but you're trading latency for load.\nThe approach is \"good enough\" for most cases—the polling interval is a tunable knob.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HuXf41dhotUEyouqAOOVt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8691.446938152854,
      "y": 2355.3099973346,
      "width": 253,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b35",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 4431204,
      "version": 302,
      "versionNonce": 496674404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GOOD : Periodic Polling",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GOOD : Periodic Polling",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "E467AoVkpi1g64XJamBX4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9397.138792840891,
      "y": 2408.915378202331,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b36",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 271732964,
      "version": 406,
      "versionNonce": 1606433252,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nEach message gets a monotonically increasing sequence number\nper chat. Clients track the last sequence number they've\nseen. If they receive message #5 but last saw #3, they know\nthey missed #4 and request a re-sync. We can generate these\nsequence numbers in a separate Redis instance with simple\nINCR (atomic increment) commands.\n\nChallenges\n\nGap detection only works when you do receive a message. If\nthe chat goes quiet after the missed message, you won't\ndetect the gap until the next message arrives. You still\nneed polling as a backstop.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nEach message gets a monotonically increasing sequence number per chat. Clients track the last sequence number they've seen. If they receive message #5 but last saw #3, they know they missed #4 and request a re-sync. We can generate these sequence numbers in a separate Redis instance with simple INCR (atomic increment) commands.\n\nChallenges\n\nGap detection only works when you do receive a message. If the chat goes quiet after the missed message, you won't detect the gap until the next message arrives. You still need polling as a backstop.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wgeYMQNHLvC1LqQvOKbkr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9398.767074568765,
      "y": 2353.5500783650473,
      "width": 495,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b37",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 654218340,
      "version": 412,
      "versionNonce": 2129091940,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GOOD : Sequence Number per chat GAP detection",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GOOD : Sequence Number per chat GAP detection",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "k715pSQgHTiXJ33bu7kv9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10132.498475712757,
      "y": 2404.888710116736,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b38",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 846620644,
      "version": 538,
      "versionNonce": 73273572,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nCombine heartbeats (from the previous section) with sequence\nnumbers:\n-> Global sequence per user: Maintain a single incrementing\ncounter per user. Every message to that user increments\ntheir sequence.\n-> Include sequence in heartbeat: When the server sends a\nheartbeat ping, include the user's current sequence number.\n-> Client detects gaps: If the client's local sequence is\nbehind the server's, it immediately requests a sync.\nThis gives you fast detection of missed messages (within one\nheartbeat interval) with minimal additional load because\nyou're already sending heartbeats.\n\nChallenges\n\nThe global sequence per user requires an atomic counter,\nwhich adds coordination. You can use Redis INCR commands,\nbut it's another dependency. The benefit is that a single\nsequence catches all missed messages regardless of which\nchat they're in.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nCombine heartbeats (from the previous section) with sequence numbers:\n-> Global sequence per user: Maintain a single incrementing counter per user. Every message to that user increments their sequence.\n-> Include sequence in heartbeat: When the server sends a heartbeat ping, include the user's current sequence number.\n-> Client detects gaps: If the client's local sequence is behind the server's, it immediately requests a sync.\nThis gives you fast detection of missed messages (within one heartbeat interval) with minimal additional load because you're already sending heartbeats.\n\nChallenges\n\nThe global sequence per user requires an atomic counter, which adds coordination. You can use Redis INCR commands, but it's another dependency. The benefit is that a single sequence catches all missed messages regardless of which chat they're in.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OOTTAy7KNPV1KYh6skSyU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10133.330077400211,
      "y": 2350.6099856157275,
      "width": 506,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b39",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 256283620,
      "version": 572,
      "versionNonce": 531780708,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485363668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GREAT : Sequence Number per chat GAP detection",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GREAT : Sequence Number per chat GAP detection",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nFP0uM35nhQpytj66SoEy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7724.615915881604,
      "y": 3082.3951916221695,
      "width": 573.6077270507812,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3B",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 532960996,
      "version": 8,
      "versionNonce": 76062684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784485608441,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How do we handle out-of-order messages?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How do we handle out-of-order messages?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0eI-itLpqli5pg7QI8MGe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7736.07132910293,
      "y": 3162.2425627338503,
      "width": 1569.79340738084,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1042799964,
      "version": 381,
      "versionNonce": 551282780,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784485779177,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Out-of-order messages are a fact of life in distributed systems and engineering such that messages are processed in the exact order they were\nsent is actually a considerable amount of additional complexity. \nWe'd need to have delays to ensure we have time for late messages to arrive and a re-ordering mechanism to handle them. \n\nNOTE : Read Flink deep dive where Flink's Bounded Out-Of-Orderness Watermark Strategy effectively waits for late messages to arrive before\nprocessing them.\n\nBut for apps like this, it's not how they work! Users would rather see new messages as quickly as possible than guarantee order. So what do we\ndo?\nAll of the Chat Servers will sync their time over NTP (Network Time Protocol). This doesn't guarantee perfect time, but it's pretty good. When\na message arrives on the Chat Server, we'll \"stamp\" it with the time it was received. Then, when clients retrieve messages, they'll have the\ntimestamp that they were received by the server. When we display messages, we display them ordered by this time. Messages have a consistent\nordering across all clients even if they arrive in a different order than they are displayed.\n\nOn occasion, this will mean a message will pop-in \"above\" another message that was actually sent later. Users find this acceptable!",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Out-of-order messages are a fact of life in distributed systems and engineering such that messages are processed in the exact order they were sent is actually a considerable amount of additional complexity. \nWe'd need to have delays to ensure we have time for late messages to arrive and a re-ordering mechanism to handle them. \n\nNOTE : Read Flink deep dive where Flink's Bounded Out-Of-Orderness Watermark Strategy effectively waits for late messages to arrive before processing them.\n\nBut for apps like this, it's not how they work! Users would rather see new messages as quickly as possible than guarantee order. So what do we do?\nAll of the Chat Servers will sync their time over NTP (Network Time Protocol). This doesn't guarantee perfect time, but it's pretty good. When a message arrives on the Chat Server, we'll \"stamp\" it with the time it was received. Then, when clients retrieve messages, they'll have the timestamp that they were received by the server. When we display messages, we display them ordered by this time. Messages have a consistent ordering across all clients even if they arrive in a different order than they are displayed.\n\nOn occasion, this will mean a message will pop-in \"above\" another message that was actually sent later. Users find this acceptable!",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-son_aiXAEBU8YndkAYgM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7719.538907703762,
      "y": 3653.9556514951532,
      "width": 616.9237060546875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1494349660,
      "version": 259,
      "versionNonce": 1654335452,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485819831,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How can we handle a \"last-seen\" functionality",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How can we handle a \"last-seen\" functionality",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "J6UqL0tptMObiJtX-XrFj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7745.716413662066,
      "y": 3800.9493344352536,
      "width": 670.5590082104189,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 787931748,
      "version": 463,
      "versionNonce": 1345660388,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485932554,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nThe naive approach is to update a lastSeen timestamp in our\ndatabase every time a user does anything: sends a message,\nreceives a message, or responds to a heartbeat.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis creates massive write amplification. With 200M\nconnected users and heartbeats every 10-30 seconds, we're\nhandling millions of writes per second just for last seen\nupdates. Even DynamoDB would struggle with this load, and\nwe'd be paying a fortune for writes that have minimal value.\nThe data is also stale immediately after writing—by the time\nyou query it, the user may have done something else. We're\npaying for strong consistency we don't need.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nThe naive approach is to update a lastSeen timestamp in our database every time a user does anything: sends a message, receives a message, or responds to a heartbeat.\n\nChallenges\n\nThis creates massive write amplification. With 200M connected users and heartbeats every 10-30 seconds, we're handling millions of writes per second just for last seen updates. Even DynamoDB would struggle with this load, and we'd be paying a fortune for writes that have minimal value.\nThe data is also stale immediately after writing—by the time you query it, the user may have done something else. We're paying for strong consistency we don't need.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FTWyci8r2cgyxr2T6r5uV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7747.344695389939,
      "y": 3745.584034597969,
      "width": 385,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1916073444,
      "version": 487,
      "versionNonce": 1635737444,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784485899405,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BAD : Write to DB on each heartbeat",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BAD : Write to DB on each heartbeat",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uB0YO16AnQq-Oz7VEIKIO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8453.036550077977,
      "y": 3799.1894154657007,
      "width": 1573.96738200892,
      "height": 1175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1533319524,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 170776676,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784486671644,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach\n\nThere's two insights we can use this to our advantage.\n-> First, when users connect to our Chat Servers, they are creating a new Websocket connection. When they disconnect (or we close the\nconnection due to missed heartbeats), we know about it.\n-> Second, if users are online they can tell us.\nSo what can we do? We'll create a new table in DynamoDB which will keep track of the last disconnect for a given user. Whenever a user\ndisconnects from a Chat Server, we'll update this value using the current timestamp. We can use DynamoDB's CONDITIONAL EXPRESSIONS (e.g., only\nupdate if the new timestamp is greater than the existing one) to ensure that two servers don't race each other and accidentally overwrite a\nmore recent disconnect time.\nNext, we'll have a special request we send from a client who wants to request a \"last seen\" a given user.\n\n// -> getLastSeen\n{\n    \"targetUserId\": \"\",\n    \"requestingUserId\": \"\",\n}\n\nWe'll have a corresponding update message\n\n// -> updateLastSeen\n{\n    \"targetUserId\": \"\",\n    \"reporter\": \"DATABASE\" | \"SERVER\",\n    \"lastSeen\": \"ONLINE\" | \"$DATE\"\n}\n\nIn order to get the last seen for a given user:\n1. The client publishes a getLastSeen message with their targetUserId and the requestingUserId.\n2. The Chat Server receives the message. In parallel, it will: \n2a) Check the LastSeen table for the targetUserId and publish a updateLastSeen message to the Pub/Sub channel for the requestingUserId. \n2b) Forward a getLastSeen message to the Pub/Sub channel for the targetUserId.\n3. If the target user's Chat Server receives the getLastSeen and the user is connected, it will publish an updateLastSeen message with lastSeen\nof \"ONLINE\" to the Pub/Sub channel for the requestingUserId.\n\nFinally, the client will merge the responses. If it receives an ONLINE message, the bubble is green. If it doesn't, it will show when the user\nlast disconnected from the service.\nThis minimizes the storage required (we only need 1 record for every user) and the number of updates (we only need to update our durable\nstorage when a user disconnects).\n\nChallenges\n\nIt's possible for there to be some delay between the two responses for an online user. We'll need the client to be able to handle this, either\nby waiting a moment before displaying the result or being able to update the UI seamlessly.\nWe are depending on Chat Servers to report disconnect times, which can be a problem if those Chat Servers fail. Fortunately, if the servers\nfail and the users are still connected, they'll reconnect shortly. If we want to be more robust, we can write to the LastSeen table when the\nconnection happens as well.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach\n\nThere's two insights we can use this to our advantage.\n-> First, when users connect to our Chat Servers, they are creating a new Websocket connection. When they disconnect (or we close the connection due to missed heartbeats), we know about it.\n-> Second, if users are online they can tell us.\nSo what can we do? We'll create a new table in DynamoDB which will keep track of the last disconnect for a given user. Whenever a user disconnects from a Chat Server, we'll update this value using the current timestamp. We can use DynamoDB's CONDITIONAL EXPRESSIONS (e.g., only update if the new timestamp is greater than the existing one) to ensure that two servers don't race each other and accidentally overwrite a more recent disconnect time.\nNext, we'll have a special request we send from a client who wants to request a \"last seen\" a given user.\n\n// -> getLastSeen\n{\n    \"targetUserId\": \"\",\n    \"requestingUserId\": \"\",\n}\n\nWe'll have a corresponding update message\n\n// -> updateLastSeen\n{\n    \"targetUserId\": \"\",\n    \"reporter\": \"DATABASE\" | \"SERVER\",\n    \"lastSeen\": \"ONLINE\" | \"$DATE\"\n}\n\nIn order to get the last seen for a given user:\n1. The client publishes a getLastSeen message with their targetUserId and the requestingUserId.\n2. The Chat Server receives the message. In parallel, it will: \n2a) Check the LastSeen table for the targetUserId and publish a updateLastSeen message to the Pub/Sub channel for the requestingUserId. \n2b) Forward a getLastSeen message to the Pub/Sub channel for the targetUserId.\n3. If the target user's Chat Server receives the getLastSeen and the user is connected, it will publish an updateLastSeen message with lastSeen of \"ONLINE\" to the Pub/Sub channel for the requestingUserId.\n\nFinally, the client will merge the responses. If it receives an ONLINE message, the bubble is green. If it doesn't, it will show when the user last disconnected from the service.\nThis minimizes the storage required (we only need 1 record for every user) and the number of updates (we only need to update our durable storage when a user disconnects).\n\nChallenges\n\nIt's possible for there to be some delay between the two responses for an online user. We'll need the client to be able to handle this, either by waiting a moment before displaying the result or being able to update the UI seamlessly.\nWe are depending on Chat Servers to report disconnect times, which can be a problem if those Chat Servers fail. Fortunately, if the servers fail and the users are still connected, they'll reconnect shortly. If we want to be more robust, we can write to the LastSeen table when the connection happens as well.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yowV-vHzIQ4DejuMA4ZaD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8454.66483180585,
      "y": 3743.824115628417,
      "width": 627,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1439943908,
      "version": 639,
      "versionNonce": 1964641380,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784486515373,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GREAT : Utilize Active Connections and CREATE a new TABLE",
      "fontSize": 20,
